    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` response is built from the generated `OwnerDto` via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, so `initials` belongs there alongside the existing computed `displayName` field.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (the source `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec), documented to match the spec.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `initials` via a small dedicated `initials(Owner)` default method rather than inlining a long expression, keeping the derivation as its own single-responsibility unit:\n\n```java\ndefault String initials(Owner owner) {\n    return Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n        + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\";\n}\n```\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` (john/smith \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full suite pass.",
